<!--
  The breaking-change inventory for this release. Generated, never hand-written
  (dotnet pack -p:ApiCompatGenerateSuppressionFile=true), which also means a regeneration drops this
  comment and the CRLF it writes needs normalising back to LF. Three entries, all deliberate:

  CP0002 WithGuards(int, int, int, int): its four parameters became int?, so a caller naming one guard
  no longer silently resets the other three to the engine constants. Source-compatible (WithGuards() and
  WithGuards(25) both still compile), binary-breaking, and 10.1.0 is the release that may carry it.

  CP0014 x2 PaginateComposedQuery&lt;TEntity&gt;.SortBy: the property and its getter lost their nullable
  annotation when a tie-breaker became mandatory at Build(), so an empty list now unambiguously means
  "resolved, nothing requested". Behavioural and source-visible to a consumer on Nullable=enable, not
  binary. They appear only because the ApiCompat attribute rule is now on: the annotation lives in
  NullableAttribute, which the signature comparison does not read and PublicAPI.Shipped.txt records
  only as line text, so the change went in with no diagnostic from anything.

  Delete this file when PackageValidationBaselineVersion moves past 10.0.3: every entry exists only
  against that baseline, and a stale suppression hides the next accidental break behind the same target.
-->
